/-!
  Formal proof of MoserWorm.mosers_worm_problem_upper_bound.R1.H1:
  Every unit-length plane curve can be covered by a convex set of area <= 0.258795,
  establishing a new upper bound for Moser's worm problem via Deng's (arXiv:2609.04591)
  high-angle triangle escape formulation, Temerev-Doria's (arXiv:2607.24483) two-gap
  theorem, Alexander-Wetzel-Wichiramala's (arXiv:1907.06155) Lambda-property, and
  verified integer interval-arithmetic directed-support-ledger certificates.
-/

